Today the rain in Mumbai is relentless.
I go out of the house.
Yesterday I brought a small umbrella.
But today I have brought my sturdy umbrella.
The roads are completely filled with water.
I board the BEST bus.
In the bus, I sit near the window.
The bus conductor comes near me.
I give him twenty rupees.
He gives me a ticket.
I say to him, 'Bhaiya, yesterday too there was a lot of rain.' 
 'Yesterday I did not see waterlogged roads.' 
 'But today I have seen only water everywhere!' 
He laughs and says, 'True, madam.' 
 'Today the roads are like rivers.' 
I look outside from the bus.
The bus goes forward slowly in the water.
I think, this is a true Mumbai monsoon experience.
